    "modules": [
      {
        "title": "Module 1: Understanding Mental Health",
        "description": "Build a strong foundation in mental health concepts.",
        "lessons": [
          {
            "title": "What is Mental Health?",
            "duration": "20 mins",
            "content": "<h2>What is Mental Health?</h2><p>Mental health refers to our emotional, psychological, and social wellbeing. It influences how we think, feel, behave, make decisions, cope with stress, and relate to others.</p><p>Good mental health does not mean feeling happy every day. It means having the ability to manage life's challenges in healthy ways.</p><h3>Learning Objectives</h3><ul><li>Define mental health</li><li>Understand emotional wellbeing</li><li>Recognize the importance of mental wellness</li></ul>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Mental Health vs Mental Illness",
            "duration": "20 mins",
            "content": "<h2>Mental Health vs Mental Illness</h2><p>Everyone has mental health, just as everyone has physical health. Mental illness refers to specific conditions that affect thinking, mood or behavior.</p><p>A person can have poor mental health without a diagnosed illness, and a person with a mental illness can still live a productive and meaningful life.</p>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Common Mental Health Myths",
            "duration": "20 mins",
            "content": "<h2>Mental Health Myths</h2><ul><li>Myth: Mental illness is a sign of weakness.</li><li>Fact: Mental illness is a health condition.</li><li>Myth: People should just 'snap out of it'.</li><li>Fact: Recovery often requires support and treatment.</li></ul>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Why Mental Health Matters",
            "duration": "25 mins",
            "content": "<h2>Why Mental Health Matters</h2><p>Mental health affects relationships, academic performance, productivity, decision-making and physical health.</p>"
          }
        ],
        "quiz": {
          "title": "Module 1 Quiz",
          "questions": 10,
          "passMark": 70
        }
